 "motifs": [],
 "notes": "A waltz-like tide in 3/4: up by step from the home note to the fifth, held across the bar, then down past the start to the leading note. Plain and singable; the held note is the high water. Winter: D minor, the theme in augmentation over open fifths, a bowed high line, and an inverted fragment to close."
